      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1784, Rockingham became Richmond County’s official seat and long served as the region’s commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carolana.com/NC/Towns/Rockingham_NC.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Downtown Rockingham is undergoing a ten‑year revitalization called “Shaping Our Future: 2023,” aiming to restore historic streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockingham%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Interstate 74 skirts two miles north of Rockingham, with a planned 13‑mile extension known as Future I‑74.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
